# scripts/build_llamacpp.sh WAS ignored here on the grounds that "the repo uses
# the upstream image". That stopped being true: the MTP result (report sections
# 11 and 15) runs on an image this script builds from the checkpoint publisher's
# fork, and section 10's arms come from an open pull request. Without it those
# sections are not reproducible, so it ships.

# raw outputs and scratch: artifacts/ is ignored by default and the runs the
# engine benchmark report actually reads are allow-listed back in below. The
# list is generated from bench/report_data.py's own globs, not hand-typed, so
# it cannot drift from what the report cites. Left out on purpose: _quarantine/
# (rejected runs), the void arms (V-01/02/03, B-22, B-23 — see artifacts/README.md),
# empty shells, and every run superseded by a later one.
artifacts/*
!artifacts/README.md
# thermal: the report reads the traces behind the full-window and ladder
# tables (section 12). The other ~148 belong to arms nobody cites.
!artifacts/thermal/
